<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6198" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calcĭtro</span></b> , ōnis,
			m.
		1. calcitro. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>One who strikes with his heels</i>, <i>a kicker</i>: equus mordax, calcitro, Varr. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. p. 45, 2</span></i> (Sat. Men. 81,
			3).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of men,
				<i>a boisterous fellow</i>, <i>a
				blusterer</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 2, 3, 11</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
